## Why Tasks Cannot Be Parallelized

- The playback route should not be implemented independently from the detail response shape, because the response determines how clients discover audio availability.
- Owner-only verification cannot run until the route exists.
- The route and verification both touch or validate the same trust boundary, so parallel edits could hide authorization regressions.

## Shared Contract Surfaces

- `server/index.mjs`
- `server/translations.mjs`
- `server/artifacts.mjs`
- `server/storage.mjs`
- API response mapping and trace/error behavior

## Cross-Epic Gates

This epic depends on Epic 02 artifact states. Epic 04 depends on `add-tts-detail-response-shape` for client types and on `verify-owner-only-artifact-access` before mobile playback uses the authenticated route.

## Recommendation

Run this epic sequentially after Epic 02, and keep playback access checks in the parent execution path.
